# The winners of ideas.bux and ideas2.bux stacked on the factorial's candidate
# (factorial.bux's r1v1k1f0p0s0: the late-2026 hybrid with hyper-connections, the
# value residual and the key-value conv on its global layers), to see whether their
# gains add up. A winner beat the candidate paired by seed at d512 (3 seeds, t > 2),
# repo_bpb_8k no worse, as architecture; Muon, zero_out and lr_floor train the model
# differently and stay out. Four did, each a factor:
#
#   E  the embedding times sqrt(d_model) (ideas2.bux's emb_sqrt, -0.73%)
#   G  GatedNorm on every branch's norm (ideas.bux's gnorm, -0.71%; it serves at 8%
#      fewer active parameters in FP8, and still wins there)
#   O  a norm of each global head's output before its gate (ideas.bux's onorm, -0.30%)
#   L  the value residual's two weights learned (ideas.bux's vres_learned, -0.13%)
#
# A half of the 2^4, of resolution IV, L = E + G + O (mod 2), so I = EGOL: no main
# effect is aliased with an interaction of two; EG = OL, EO = GL, EL = GO. Its first
# cell is the candidate itself, which factorial.bux ran. ideas.bux and ideas2.bux ran
# the four singles, in the other half; with them and s3_e1g0o1l1, every factor is
# also seen alone on the candidate. s3_e1g1o1l1 is all four, s3_e1g0o1l1 the three
# that cost nothing to serve.
#
#   arm          E G O L
#   (candidate)  0 0 0 0   factorial.bux's r1v1k1f0p0s0
#   s3_e1g0o0l1  1 0 0 1
#   s3_e0g1o0l1  0 1 0 1
#   s3_e0g0o1l1  0 0 1 1
#   s3_e1g1o0l0  1 1 0 0
#   s3_e1g0o1l0  1 0 1 0
#   s3_e0g1o1l0  0 1 1 0
#   s3_e1g1o1l1  1 1 1 1   all four
#   s3_e1g0o1l1  1 0 1 1   off the design: those cheap to serve
#
# The residual is hc in every arm, every branch's, the MTP module's too; the MTP
# module keeps the hybrid's layer, as each winner's own arm did.
use m2026_hybrid
use timeline_code
use rungs

emb_s      = embed(scale_by_sqrt_dim=true)
gated_norm = fr_norm (_ * (linear(features=16) swish linear(features=d_model) sigmoid))
g_l        = fr_global(kv_conv_size=4, value_residual=learned)
g_o        = fr_global(kv_conv_size=4, output_norm=fr_norm)
g_ol       = fr_global(kv_conv_size=4, output_norm=fr_norm, value_residual=learned)

# The candidate with x as its embedding, n as its branches' norm and g as its global
# layers, the first of which gives its values to the rest.
lay(n, mixer, ffn=fr_experts) = [n mixer] [n ffn]
stack(x, n, g) = x
                 lay(n, hy_delta, fr_dense) lay(n, hy_delta)^2 lay(n, g(v=@v1))
                 (lay(n, hy_delta)^3 lay(n, g(v=$v1)))^(layers // 4 - 1)
                 fr_norm @h fr_out hy_mtp

model = s3_e1g0o0l1: stack(emb_s, fr_norm, g_l)
      | s3_e0g1o0l1: stack(embed, gated_norm, g_l)
      | s3_e0g0o1l1: stack(embed, fr_norm, g_ol)
      | s3_e1g1o0l0: stack(emb_s, gated_norm, fr_global(kv_conv_size=4))
      | s3_e1g0o1l0: stack(emb_s, fr_norm, g_o)
      | s3_e0g1o1l0: stack(embed, gated_norm, g_o)
      | s3_e1g1o1l1: stack(emb_s, gated_norm, g_ol)
      | s3_e1g0o1l1: stack(emb_s, fr_norm, g_ol)

residual = s3_e1g0o0l1: hc(expansion=4) | s3_e0g1o0l1: hc(expansion=4)
         | s3_e0g0o1l1: hc(expansion=4) | s3_e1g1o0l0: hc(expansion=4)
         | s3_e1g0o1l0: hc(expansion=4) | s3_e0g1o1l0: hc(expansion=4)
         | s3_e1g1o1l1: hc(expansion=4) | s3_e1g0o1l1: hc(expansion=4)

# The hybrid's best at d512 (milestones.bux's scan), for every arm.
optimizer.lr = 2e-3
